# ===== ChatGPT pro mining source pack =====
# The corpus itself is public domain - Ramanujan's notebooks, his own published
# papers (ram01-37), and the 1927 Collected Papers - fetched from
# ramanujan.sirinudi.org and archive.org. It is committed so the mining runs
# stay reproducible.
#
# These third-party papers are still in copyright and must NOT be redistributed
# from a public repo. They are fetchable from the manifests if you need them.
chatgpt-pro-mining/**/quarterly_reports/
chatgpt-pro-mining/**/open_access_context_pdfs/*
!chatgpt-pro-mining/**/open_access_context_pdfs/collected_papers_of_srinivasa_ramanujan_1927_internet_archive_scan.pdf

# ===== Secrets / API keys =====
# Datalab Chandra 2 API key etc. NEVER commit.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# ===== CLI tool working-state directories =====
# agy (Gemini CLI) writes UUID-keyed working memory under brain/
brain/

# ===== Python =====
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ===== macOS / editors =====
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# ===== Primary-source scans (large facsimile PDFs) =====
# Per the original convention: anything >1MB under corpora/scans/ stays local.
# Pin specific extensions rather than the whole directory so manifests/READMEs commit.
corpora/scans/**/*.pdf
corpora/scans/**/*.png
corpora/scans/**/*.jpg
corpora/scans/**/*.jpeg
corpora/scans/**/*.tif
corpora/scans/**/*.tiff

# ===== Vendored 3rd-party working state =====
corpora/RamanujanMachine/source/venv/
corpora/RamanujanMachine/source/__pycache__/
corpora/RamanujanMachine/source/tmp_results/

# ===== Experiment outputs that are large or regeneratable =====
# Keep small CSVs in analysis/results/ (they're the durable record).
# But ignore stray heavy artifacts:
*.log
*.tmp
